         DuckDB: Agg over 1 leaf
         DuckDB SQL: SELECT * FROM (SELECT n1.c1 AS c1, CAST(count(*) AS BIGINT) AS c2 FROM (SELECT * FROM gg_leaf(0)) AS n1 GROUP BY n1.c1) AS n2 ORDER BY c1 ASC NULLS LAST
         ->  Seq Scan on public.d_orders
               Output: d_orders.id
               Filter: (d_orders.id < 30)
 Optimizer: GPORCA
 Settings: effective_cache_size = '512MB', gp_enable_multiphase_agg = 'off'
(11 rows)

