EXPLAIN (COSTS OFF)
SELECT d.id, count(*), sum(o.qty), sum(o.amount), min(o.id), max(o.id), max(o.big), max(o.ts)
  FROM d_orders o JOIN d_dim d ON o.cust = d.id WHERE d.grp = 1 GROUP BY d.id;
NOTICE:  gg_duckdb: Agg (plan node 1): the cost gate prefers the standard executor
NOTICE:  gg_duckdb: Agg (plan node 4): the cost gate prefers the standard executor
NOTICE:  gg_duckdb: HashJoin (plan node 5): the cost gate prefers the standard executor
                                   QUERY PLAN                                    
